Cooperative-learning engine vendored from the R package multiview (GPL-2).

Upstream authors:
  Daisy Yi Ding, Robert J. Tibshirani, Balasubramanian Narasimhan,
  Trevor Hastie, Kenneth Tay, James Yang, Jonathan Taylor

Source: CRAN multiview version 1.0 (2026-05-11)
https://cran.r-project.org/package=multiview
Upstream source tarball SHA-256:
91ba5b33170392a6298d4d1bb9b051df5ade412aa55ff7fe4ae2c89ff833f9d5

Imported files:
  R/cooperative-*.R (renamed from the upstream R sources),
  src/wls_exp.cpp, src/driver.h, and src/glmnetpp/.

Local modifications:
  upstream R symbols were given the cooperative- file prefix; calls were
  adapted to the stablr namespace and manual cooperative S3 registrations;
  a stablr-facing backend and validation/provenance layer were added; and the
  native registration/build files were integrated with stablr. Algorithmic
  cooperative-learning code remains derived from multiview 1.0.

  Four silent upstream-bug fixes diverge from byte-parity with multiview
  1.0 (all verified correct; all unreachable or zero-impact in-package
  because the backend never exposes `offset`):
  1. cooperative-multiview.path.R (~:770): in the IRLS step-halving
     branch the warm-residual update is
     `w_std * (target - g_eta + g_offset)` — upstream multiview 1.0 has
     `w_std * (target - g_eta) + g_offset` at the equivalent site while
     its sibling site (~:659) uses the offset-inside form in both
     codebases; upstream is internally inconsistent and the vendored
     copy uses the consistent form.
  2. cooperative-multiview.path.R (~:683): the warm-started `elnet.fit`
     call propagates `lower.limits`; upstream drops it on IRLS
     iterations >= 2.
  3. cooperative-multiview.R (~:251): `if (length(rho) != 1L || rho < 0)`
     fixes an upstream typo `if (rho < 0 || length(row) != 1L)` (`row`
     resolves to `base::row`, so upstream never rejects vector `rho`).
  4. cooperative-build_predmat.R (~:26): `offset_sub <- offset[which,
     drop = FALSE]` fixes upstream `offset_sub <- rep(offset_sub[which,
     drop = FALSE])`, which references `offset_sub` before it exists and
     crashes on any CV fit with non-NULL offset.

  Additionally, the unexported, unregistered, and uncalled upstream
  `coef_ordered` generic and its `coef_ordered.multiview` /
  `coef_ordered.cv.multiview` methods were removed as dead code
  (2026-10-20, implementation-review batch F-3).

